This package is a new extraction of Linux-visible io_uring policy and
lifecycle contracts designed for TheKernel and distributed under Apache-2.0.

Linux, liburing, and Asterinas sources were consulted to understand observable
ABI, memory-ordering, request, resource, completion, cancellation, and teardown
contracts. No liburing or Asterinas source text is in this package; liburing was
read for caller-side semantics only, and no liburing reference tree is recorded
in this repository, so that statement is asserted rather than scanned.

Copied text: this package does quote Linux. Measured against the Linux 7.2.3
tree with `scripts/ci/scan_linux_excerpts.py` (whitespace-normalised lines of at
least 40 characters, byte-identical to a Linux `*.c` line): 18 lines of verbatim
Linux text in 2 files — 1 inside a fenced doc block and 17 in unfenced `//`
comment blocks — and 25 such lines at the inclusive 25-character threshold, all
24 of the additional ones outside fences.

* `src/registration.rs:442-443` — the fenced block at `:441-444` quotes the
  `io_uring_register()` blind-dispatch test as two Linux lines, of which only
  `:443` is long enough to count; the pair is `io_uring/register.c:1031-1032`
  in the 7.2.3 tree, and the prose cites say so (`:397`, `:446`) — earlier they
  read `:1029-1030`, which is a different statement.
* `src/registration.rs` — 16 more verbatim lines at the 40-character threshold,
